System prompt: "You should always follow the instructions and output a valid JSON object. Please use the specified JSON object structure according to the instructions. If unsure, please default to using {"answer":"$your_answer"}. Ensure to always use "```"End the code block to indicate the end of the JSON object."

Then the rest of the system prompt says output one JSON object and nothing else, no prose, no code fence. There's a conflict within the system prompt itself. The later part (the memory patch instructions) is more specific: "one JSON object and nothing else, no prose, no code fence, matching this JSON schema". I'll follow the more specific later instruction: no code fence. Hmm, but "Ensure to always use ``` to End the code block" is explicit too. Given the schema instruction explicitly says "no code fence", I'll go without code fence. Actually, to hedge, many of these tasks expect pure JSON. I'll output pure JSON.

Output:

{
 "add_facts": [
  {
   "content": "The indexer depends on the product catalog for product documents.",
   "entities": ["indexer", "product catalog"],
   "kind": "fact",
   "confidence": 1,
   "evidence": "the search indexer needs the product catalog (product documents)"
  }
 ],
 "add_relations": [
  {
   "src": "indexer",
   "dst": "product catalog",
   "rel_kind": "depends_on",
   "evidence": "the search indexer needs the product catalog (product documents)"
  }
 ],
 "entity_aliases": [
  {
   "name": "search indexer",
   "canonical": "indexer",
   "evidence": "the search indexer needs the product catalog"
  }
 ]
}

